ASSEMBLY LAB 2 - REGISTER SAVE/RESTORE

Source adapted from userland/examples/asm/03-stack.s.
Write /tmp/stack.s:

  movs r4, #7
  push {r4}
  movs r4, #0
  pop {r4}
  movs r0, #3
  movs r1, #0
  svc #0

Run: as /tmp/stack.s ; then /tmp/a.out.
Expected: no stdout; returns with status 0.

The demo saves r4 onto the task stack and restores it.
Do not omit the exit syscall: there is no ordinary main() return.
The stack has a 4 KiB reservation, shared with call frames.
Do not perform intentionally unbalanced push/pop on real hardware.
See /man/languages/asm for accepted register lists.
